<title>FRANCE: France still awaits U.N. word on Iraq wheat deals.</title>
<headline>France still awaits U.N. word on Iraq wheat deals.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>France is still waiting for the U.N. to approve wheat sales contracts to Iraq signed by French companies in December, a French official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The contracts, for 300,000 tonnes of French wheat, were the first French grain sales to Iraq under a scheme allowing Baghdad to sell oil in exchange for food and medicine.</p>
<p>&quot;The U.N. has still not replied. It is making studies,&quot; the official from the French budget ministry told Reuters.</p>
<p>He could not say when the U.N. committee responsible for vetting such deals was expected to give its reply.</p>
<p>Shipments of the grain were due to have started in January and continued in February.</p>
<p>Since that grain was sold, French companies have sold up to 275,000 tonnes more wheat to Iraq for shipment in March and April.</p>
<p>The French official said the companies involved in those most recent deals had not yet asked the government to forward applications for their approval to the U.N.</p>
</text>
